// NDJSON-only spec: behaviour that exists because NDJSON omits absent fields entirely.
//
// Every other format carries a column in every file -- a CSV header names it even when every value is
// null, and Parquet/ORC keep it in the schema. NDJSON does not: a record simply has no key. So a file
// can genuinely contain NONE of the columns a query projects, which is a state no other format can
// reach, and it is why these cases cannot live in the shared external-hive-partitioned-shadow spec.

// A hive partition whose files omit the partition column entirely (the __HIVE_DEFAULT_PARTITION__
// bucket) is still read, and the absent column reads null there with a warning naming it.
//
// This pins the fix for elastic/esql-planning#1791: split discovery used to drop a whole file when it
// shared no column with the projection, silently losing its rows. The 10 rows counted under `null`
// below are that file. Without this case the fix has no test in this corpus -- the shared spec cannot
// carry it, because no other format emits the warning.
sparsePartitionFileIsReadAndWarnsForTheAbsentColumn
required_capability: dataset_in_from_command
dataset: employees_hive_shadow_sparse: "{{employees_hive_shadow}}" WITH {"partition_detection": "none"}

FROM employees_hive_shadow_sparse
| STATS count = COUNT(*) BY languages
| SORT languages NULLS LAST;
warningRegex:declared column \[languages\] is not present in some source files and reads null there

count:long | languages:integer
15         | 1
19         | 2
17         | 3
18         | 4
21         | 5
10         | null
;
